===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[penalty]] [[box]]|es}}

# {{lb|en|ice hockey}} An enclosed bench where a player must remain for timed period (a [[penalty]]) that is assessed after an infraction.
#: ''Both players got to cool their heels for five minutes in their respective '''penalty boxes''' after the fight.''
# {{lb|en|soccer}} The [[penalty area]].
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|figuratively}} A temporary [[punishment]], or, metaphorically, a similar setback (e.g., loss of control, embarrassment, etc.).
#* '''2003''', Tim Breithaupt, ''10 Steps to Sales Success: The Proven System That Can Shorten the Selling Cycle, Double Your Close Ratio'', ISBN 081447165X, [http://books.google.com/books?id=9yNSqTdMjZ0C&pg=PA174&dq=%22penalty+box%22+-hockey+-football+-soccer&sig=zWYjAqASux2QhQp119WmnxRE5iI#PPA170,M1 pg. 170]:
#*: A visit to the '''penalty box''' occurs when the salesman has relinquished control of the sales call by immediately answering the customer's question.
#* '''2003''', John Portmann, ''Sex and heaven: Catholics in bed and at prayer'', ISBN 0312294883, [http://books.google.com/books?id=xwNXacL5gtkC&pg=PA155&dq=%22penalty+box%22+-hockey+-football+-soccer&sig=9h4AXhHiftBJezXQ9EwY6UYhqcI pg. 155]:
#*: What can land you in this metaphorical holding cell, the '''penalty box''' of Catholicism?
#* '''2008''', John Zarrella and Patrick Oppmann, "Florida, Michigan seek exit from Democratic penalty box," CNN.com, [http://www.cnn.com/2008/POLITICS/03/06/florida.michigan/index.html]:
#*: Florida, Michigan seek exit from Democratic '''penalty box'''

